A filament lamp is non-ohmic \emph{in normal operation}: increasing the p.d. increases its temperature as well as its current, so the physical conditions are not being held constant and $V/I$ changes. This observation does not show that tungsten disobeys Ohm's law at a fixed temperature. For any device, $V/I$ can still be calculated at one operating point; for a non-linear $V$--$I$ curve, however, that ratio is not one constant valid at every point.

